# Cursor subagent models

When using the Task tool — including `mult`, `orchestrate`, or any subagent spawn — pass only:

- `cursor-grok-4.6-high` for quality work
- `composer-2.5-fast` for deterministic work
- `inherit` if the parent is already that model

Never pass `claude-opus-5-thinking-high`, `claude-opus-5`, other `claude-*`, `gpt-5.6-*`, `gpt-5.3-codex`, `gemini-3.1-pro`, `glm-5.2-high`, or `kimi-k3-max`, even if Task lists them.

If the `orchestrate` SKILL.md you opened names Opus, Luna, Terra, or Sol, you opened the Claude or Codex copy. Read `${HOME}/.cursor/skills/orchestrate/SKILL.md` and follow that instead.

Do not add this rule to `AGENTS.md` (Claude/Codex must keep their own spawn tables).
